<title>ESTONIA: HANSAPANK FIRST QUARTER PROFIT SOARS.</title>
<headline>HANSAPANK FIRST QUARTER PROFIT SOARS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia's Hansapank, the largest bank in the Baltics, said on Friday that its first quarter profit had soared to 96.4 million kroons versus 36.7 million kroons in the same period last year.</p>
<p>The bank also said in a statement that its profit in March was 22.4 million kroons versus 22.0 million kroons in February.</p>
<p>--David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 6 30 84 00, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
